Edrobot wrote:
> I almost never get far in the Gnomish Mines, so today I am going to
> try going somewhat down in the main branch first.
> 
> Is that wise?

Depends on many factors. A plus is having a light source (or lit mine
levels). A plus is being lawful to find most dwarfs peaceful. A plus
is having good AC because you may easily be surrounded there. A plus
is to be poison resistant (poisoned arrows and wands may hit you and
you often are in an exposed position there).

> Any other hints?

If the mines is hostile environment it may be better to wait on the
stairs (climbing up if necessary to heal) until you collected a fine
armor set before you completely explore the first mine level. Another
option is continuing the main branch and doing Sokoban first.

It really depends on many factors.

